From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 23:59:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2952/3799] soh: rename func_80984F10 -> DemoIm_TrackPlayerHead

Name source: DEDUCED from the code (confidence HIGH) -- zeldaret/oot
leaves this symbol address-named too, so there is no upstream name to adopt.
Reason: head and torso tracking with a 12-unit eye offset
Defined in soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_Demo_Im/z_demo_im.c.

Tagged [LLM:HIGH] at the definition, every declaration and every call site, so a
reader meeting the name anywhere knows it is inferred.
---
 soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_Demo_Im/z_demo_im.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_Demo_Im/z_demo_im.c b/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_Demo_Im/z_demo_im.c
index 5362fb24f..8f700665f 100644
--- a/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_Demo_Im/z_demo_im.c
+++ b/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_Demo_Im/z_demo_im.c
@@ -196,7 +196,8 @@ void DemoIm_TrackPlayerWithinAngle(DemoIm* this, PlayState* play) {
     Npc_TrackPoint(&this->actor, &this->interactInfo, kREG(17) + 0xC, npcTrackingMode);
 }
 
-void func_80984F10(DemoIm* this, PlayState* play) {
+// LLM generated name (HIGH), was func_80984F10: head and torso tracking with a 12-unit eye offset
+void DemoIm_TrackPlayerHead(DemoIm* this, PlayState* play) {
     Player* player = GET_PLAYER(play);
 
     this->interactInfo.trackPos = player->actor.world.pos;
@@ -556,7 +557,7 @@ void func_80985E60(DemoIm* this, PlayState* play) {
 
 void func_80985EAC(DemoIm* this, PlayState* play) {
     if ((play->csCtx.frames >= 80) && (play->csCtx.frames < 243)) {
-        func_80984F10(this, play);
+        DemoIm_TrackPlayerHead(this, play);  // was func_80984F10 [LLM:HIGH]
     } else {
         DemoIm_ReturnHeadToNeutral(this);  // was func_80984DB8 [LLM:HIGH]
     }
